 "change": "NTSDAndroidApp.extract created each directory and copied each of the ~1,900 assets one after another, reading an asset in 64 KB chunks into a growing Data. It now creates the directories first (in the list's order), then copies the files on every core with OriginalConcurrentInputs.threadLoop, each asset read once into a buffer of its length and written from it; the first failing file in the list's order is reported and the marker is still written last. load_memory.py gains --fresh-data (removes the extraction marker before each launch).",
 "fresh": "load_memory.py --fresh-data A/B (ml-s2-fresh-ab, S2 L19 S2 L19 S2): startupSeconds S2 16.78, 18.61, 16.75 against L19 26.63, 22.75 (median 24.7 -> 16.8 s); start to loaded 26.4-28.4 against 32.3-36.1 s. The window includes deleting the previous copy; writing 726 MB to the A12's flash bounds it.",
 "review": "independent read-only reviewer: no bug on the success path; when extraction fails, a different file can be named (out of space: files now fill the disk together; directories created first), and reads stop at the asset's length (Android's reader stops there); up to ~100 MB buffered at once while the last, largest files (music) are copied, before the game loads; follow-ups applied before the gate: the comment, buffers not zero-filled",
